course: dictionary
lesson: 5728
title: Lord: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Lord has four main meanings. A lord is a man of high rank, like Lord Smith. A lord can also be a man with power over others, like the lord of a castle in history.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The French-speaking lord's table» is about power and rank in old England, but «I will confess my transgressions to the Lord» means God. Ask yourself which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Lord also works as a shout. «Lord!» or «Good Lord!» shows surprise or worry, but some people find it disrespectful, so think about who is listening. Lord can also be part of a phrase: to lord it over someone means to act bossy and superior.
fact: A lord is a man of high rank, especially a noble in the UK, such as Lord Smith.
fact: In history, a lord was a man with power over others, like the lord of a castle.
fact: The Lord, with a capital L, is a name for God in Christianity.
fact: «Lord!» or «Good Lord!» is an exclamation that shows surprise or worry.
fact: «Lord it over someone» means to act bossy and superior.
exercise: «The French-speaking lord's table was full of food.» What does lord mean here? | *A man of high rank with power over others | A kind of tall tree | The Lord, the name for God | An exclamation of surprise
exercise: «I will confess my transgressions to the Lord.» Which meaning of lord is this? | *The name for God in Christianity | An exclamation of surprise | A man of high rank in the UK | A bossy way to act
exercise: Sam shouts «Good Lord!» when he sees the broken window. What does the word show? | That he is a noble | That he wants to be a lord | Happiness at a party | *Surprise or worry
test: «Lord Smith was invited to the palace.» What does lord mean here? | A wall around a castle | The name for God | *A man of high rank, with a title | An exclamation of surprise
test: «She would not let her brother lord it over her.» What does lord it over mean? | Tell a story about a castle | Be kind and gentle | Shout in surprise | *Act bossy and superior
exam: Some people say «Good Lord!» is disrespectful. What is the best tip when you use lord as an exclamation? | Use it only when you are a lord | *Think about who is listening and be careful | Only use it in church | Shout it loudly so everyone hears
